{title: Rocky Top}
{artist: Felice and Boudleaux Bryant}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]Wish that I was [F]on ole [C]Rocky Top [Am]down in the [G]Tennessee [C]hills
[C]Ain't no smoggy [F]smoke on [C]Rocky Top, [Am]ain't no [G]telephone [C]bills

[C]Once I had a [F]girl on [C]Rocky Top, [Am]half bear the [G]other half [C]cat
[C]Wild as a mink as [F]sweet as [C]soda pop, [Am]I still [G]dream about [C]that

{comment: Chorus}
[Am]Rocky Top, you'll [G]always be [Bb]home sweet home to [F]me
Good ole [C]Rocky Top - Rocky Top [Bb]Tenne[C]ssee, Rocky Top [Bb]Tenne[C]ssee

{comment: Break}

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]Once two strangers [F]climbed ole [C]Rocky Top [Am]lookin' for a [G]moonshine [C]still.
[C]Strangers ain't come [F]down from [C]Rocky Top, [Am]reckon they [G]never [C]will.

[C]Corn won't grow at [F]all on [C]Rocky Top, [Am]dirt's too [G]rocky by [C]far.
[C]That's why all the [F]folks on [C]Rocky Top [Am]get their [G]corn from a [C]jar.

{comment: Chorus}
{comment: Break}

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]I've had years of [F]cramped up [C]city life; [Am]stuck like a [G]duck in a [C]pen.
[C]All I know is [F]it's a pity [C]life can't be [Am]simple a[G]gain.[C]

{comment: Chorus}
